(*!
<summary>
Beckhoff 3-phase power measurement input channel process image.
</summary>
<description>
Represents EL3413/EL3433 phase PDO 0x1A00, 0x1A01 or 0x1A02, including mandatory channel Status.
Status contains voltage/current limits, phase sequence, missing zero crossing, TxPDO State and Toggle.
Reject data when Status bit 14 is set; bit 15 toggles on update. Evaluate bus validity as well.
Current is signed in 0.000001 A, Voltage in 0.0001 V and ActivePower in 0.01 W before transformer ratios.
Index acknowledges the selection for VariantValue; do not interpret it using only the requested output Index.
Indices 0..5 select apparent power (0.01 VA), reactive power (0.01 var), energy (0.001 Wh), power factor
(0.001), frequency (0.1 Hz) and negative energy (0.001 Wh). Further indices depend on device firmware.
EL3403 uses EL3403_INPUT_CHANNEL because its phase status differs. Link fields individually, not as a wire buffer.
Use one owner task and synchronize other access; copies do not guarantee an atomic snapshot.
When used for I/O, link located fields or their containing buffers to the matching selected PDOs.
The record is not a packed wire buffer; compiler padding is not part of the device specification.
Unlinked/default values do not prove valid I/O. The caller evaluates bus/channel validity before use.
Use one owner task per instance and externally synchronize other access; multi-field snapshots are not atomic.
Copies store data without creating hardware links. Keep borrowed field references valid while consumers are bound.
This passive record performs no validation, synchronization, configuration or protocol advancement.
</description>
*)
TYPE POWER_MEASUREMENT_INPUT_CHANNEL :
STRUCT
	//! <summary>Phase status; TxPDO State bit 14 invalidates data and bit 15 toggles on update.</summary>
	Status AT %I* : WORD;
	Current AT %I* : DINT;
	Voltage AT %I* : DINT;
	ActivePower AT %I* : DINT;
	Index AT %I* : USINT;
	VariantValue AT %I* : DINT;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>
